/block></next></block></statement></block><block type=\"gameinterval\" x=\"4011\" y=\"1439\"><comment pinned=\"false\" h=\"80\" w=\"160\">Reference: https://arcade.makecode.com/reference/sprites/sprite/vx\nThe \"Go to each side\" example reverses horizontal movement by changing vx.\nMy code checks left &lt;= 0 or right &gt;= 160 only while the fish moves outwards,puts its edge back on the boundary, then changes vx to point into the screen.\nReference: https://arcade.makecode.com/reference/sprites/sprite/vy\nThe reference explains vertical movement: my code reverses vy at 0 and 120 too.\nThese position and direction checks make the big fish bounce back at each edge.\nReference: https://arcade.makecode.com/reference/images/image/flip-x\nThe reference flips an image left-to-right. My code uses big_fish_facing_left with vx to flip once per turn, keeping the picture facing its swimming direction.\n============================================================================================================================================================================\n============================================================================================================================================================================\n24. SPAWN KILLER WHALE\nWhales can appear before the shark reaches level 3.\nThe level controls whether the shark can eat a whale, not whether a whale can appear.\nIf a whale is still present at the next 8 second check, no extra whale is created.</comment><value name=\"period\"><shadow type=\"timePicker\"><field name=\"ms\">8000</field></shadow></value><statement name=\"HANDLER\"><block type=\"typescript_statement\"><mutation xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" line0=\"let vertical_speed3: number;\" numlines=\"1\" declaredvars=\"vertical_speed3\"></mutation><next><block type=\"controls_if\"><value name=\"IF0\"><shadow type=\"logic_boolean\"><field name=\"BOOL\">TRUE</field></shadow><block type=\"logic_compare\"><field name=\"OP\">EQ<