00</field></shadow></value><next><block type=\"variables_set\"><field name=\"VAR\" id=\"Quy^%gw@YD8:xGD#l62e\">can_take_damage</field><value name=\"VALUE\"><shadow type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">0</field></shadow><block type=\"logic_boolean\"><field name=\"BOOL\">TRUE</field></block></value></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></statement></block></statement></block><block type=\"function_definition\" x=\"1861\" y=\"2858\"><mutation name=\"play_growth_sound\" functionid=\"II5lTnWuqqmQVC,xllKK\"></mutation><field name=\"function_name\">play_growth_sound</field><comment pinned=\"false\" h=\"80\" w=\"160\">Reference: https://arcade.makecode.com/reference/info/on-countdown-end\nThe reference runs a function when the countdown reaches zero.\nMy code registers on_countdown_end to play the ending sound, read the score, show it in a message, and finish the game with game.game_over(True). (game over screen)\nReference: https://arcade.makecode.com/reference/info/high-score\nThe reference retrieves the recorded best score with info.high_score().\nMy code saves it before the run and compares final_score against that value.\nA higher score, or a previous best of 0, selects \"NEW HIGH SCORE!\"\notherwise the message challenges the player to beat the previous best score.\n============================================================================================================================================================================\n============================================================================================================================================================================\nReference: https://arcade.makecode.com/reference/music/play-tone\n7. GROWTH SOUND</comment><statement name=\"STACK\"><block type=\"mixer_play_note\"><value name=\"note\"><shadow type=\"device_note\"><field name=\"note\">523</field></shadow></value><value name=\"duration\"><shadow type=\"device_beat\"><field name=\"fraction\">BeatFraction.Half</field></shadow><block type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">70</field></block></value><next><block type=\"mixer_play_note\"><value name=\"note\"><shadow type=\"device_note\"><field name=\"note\">659</field></shadow></value><value name=\"duration\"><shadow type=\"device_beat\"><field name=\"fraction\">BeatFraction.Half</field></shadow><block type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">70</field></block></value><next><block type=\"mixer_play_note\"><value name=\"note\"><shadow type=\"device_note\"><field name=\"note\">784</field></shadow></value><value name=\"duration\"><shadow type=\"device_beat\"><field name=\"fraction\">BeatFraction.Half</field></shadow><block type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">130</field></block></value></block></next></block></next></block></statement></block><block type=\"function_definition\" x=\"2243\" y=\"2858\"><mutation name=\"play_whale_sound\" functionid=\"$oI[!GM$]W(or4nl?y^}\"></mutation><field name=\"function_name\">play_whale_sound</field><comment pinned=\"false\" h=\"80\" w=\"160\">The reference explains how frequency controls pitch and milliseconds control length.\nMy code uses falling pitches of 523, 392 and 262 Hz for 120, 120 and 250 ms.\nThe longer final tone marks the end of the two minute countdown.\n============================================================================================================================================================================\n============================================================================================================================================================================\n9. KILLER WHALE SOUND</comment><statement name=\"STACK\"><block type=\"mixer_play_note\"><value name=\"note\"><shadow type=\"device_note\"><field name=\"note\">523</field></shadow></value><value name=\"duration\"><shadow type=\"device_beat\"><field name=\"fraction\">BeatFraction.Half</field></shadow><block type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">70</field></block></value><next><block type=\"mixer_play_note\"><value name=\"note\"><shadow type=\"device_note\"><field name=\"note\">784</field></shadow></value><value name=\"duration\"><shadow type=\"device_beat\"><field name=\"fraction\">BeatFraction.Half</field></shadow><block type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">70</field></block></value><next><block type=\"mixer_play_note\"><value name=\"note\"><shadow type=\"device_note\"><field name=\"note\">1047</field></shadow></value><value name=\"duration\"><shadow type=\"device_beat\"><field name=\"fraction\">BeatFraction.Half</field></shadow><block type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">130</field></block></value></block></next></block></next></block></statement></block><block type=\"function_definition\" x=\"2630\" y=\"2858\"><mutation name=\"change_shark_image\" functionid=\"zs;e#~YE{1,j79AZUmD+\"><arg name=\"new_image\" id=\"a3zsfd7kkoog1zfealzc\" type=\"Image\"></arg></mutation><field name=\"function_name\">change_shark_image</field><comment pinned=\"false\" h=\"80\" w=\"160\">Reference: https://arcade.makecode.com/reference/sprites/on-overlap\nThe reference runs a handler when two chosen sprite kinds touch.\nMy code selects player and KillerWhale, then checks shark_level:\nlevel 3 eats the whale for 10 points: lower levels take damage without removing the whale.\nReference: https://arcade.makecode.com/reference/info/change-life-by\nThe reference adds life with positive values and removes it with negative values.\nMy code uses 1 for eating and -1 for damage, with a separate 3 heart cap.\nThe shared can_take_damage flag and pause also protect against repeated hits.\n============================================================================================================================================================================\n============================================================================================================================================================================\n11. CHANGE