0\">Reference: https://arcade.makecode.com/reference/game/on-update-interval\nThe reference repeats a function at a set interval: my code uses 8000 for 8 seconds.\nReference: https://arcade.makecode.com/reference/sprites/all-of-kind\nThe reference lists sprites of a chosen kind. My code creates a KillerWhale only when that list is empty, preventing multiple whales from spawning together.\nReference: https://arcade.makecode.com/reference/sprites/sprite/set-flag\nThe reference explains AutoDestroy: my code sets it False to keep the whale from being removed offscreen before the movement code can turn it back.\nIts starting velocity is -45 horizontally, with a random vertical speed of 15-30.\n============================================================================================================================================================================\n25. HUNGER SYSTEM\nThis is a separate repeating timer from the twominute game countdown.\nIt does not check can_take_damage, so protection from fish or whale hits\ndoes not stop hunger from removing a heart.</comment><value name=\"period\"><shadow type=\"timePicker\"><field name=\"ms\">10000</field></shadow></value><statement name=\"HANDLER\"><block type=\"hudChangeLifeBy\"><value name=\"value\"><shadow type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">-1</field></shadow></value></block></statement></block><block type=\"spritesoverlap\" x=\"5307\" y=\"1439\"><comment pinned=\"false\" h=\"80\" w=\"160\">The reference explains the pitch and duration inputs for music.play_tone().\nMy code calls it twice: 659 Hz for 70 ms, then 880 Hz for 100 ms.\nThe rising sound plays when the shark eats a big fish.\n============================================================================================================================================================================\n=========================================================================================================================================================