erlap\" x=\"931\" y=\"2858\"><comment pinned=\"false\" h=\"80\" w=\"160\">The reference shows how to choose the pitch and length of a tone.\nMy code combines 523, 784 and 1047 Hz for 70, 70 and 130 ms.\nThis separate sound plays when the level 3 shark eats a killer whale.\n=======================================================================g=====================================================================================================\n============================================================================================================================================================================\n10. KILLER WHALE COLLISION\nThe whale is food at level 3, but it is dangerous at levels 1 and 2.\nIt uses the same can_take_damage setting as the big fish.\nWhile that setting is False, neither creature can take another heart through these touch rules.</comment><value name=\"HANDLER_DRAG_PARAM_sprite\"><block type=\"argument_reporter_custom\" deletable=\"false\"><mutation typename=\"Sprite\"></mutation><field name=\"VALUE\">player_sprite2</field></block></value><value name=\"kind\"><shadow type=\"spritekind\"><field name=\"MEMBER\">Player</field></shadow></value><value name=\"HANDLER_DRAG_PARAM_otherSprite\"><block type=\"argument_reporter_custom\" deletable=\"false\"><mutation typename=\"Sprite\"></mutation><field name=\"VALUE\">touched_whale</field></block></value><value name=\"otherKind\"><shadow type=\"spritekind\"><field name=\"MEMBER\">KillerWhale</field></shadow></value><statement name=\"HANDLER\"><block type=\"controls_if\"><mutation elseif=\"1\"></mutation><value name=\"IF0\"><shadow type=\"logic_boolean\"><field name=\"BOOL\">TRUE</field></shadow><block type=\"logic_compare\"><field name=\"OP\">GTE</field><value name=\"A\"><shadow type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">0</field></shadow><block type=\"variables_get\"><field name=\"VAR\" id=\"_3Z|YeDQ8X$~o-61(Eve\">shark_level</field></block></value><value name=\"B\"><shadow type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">3</field></shadow></value></block></value><statement name=\"DO0\"><block type=\"spritedestroy2\"><mutation xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" _expanded=\"0\" _input_init=\"true\"></mutation><field name=\"effect\">effects.spray</field><value name=\"sprite\"><block type=\"variables_get\"><field name=\"VAR\" id=\"%U})#eF{-43Y:k|ZA+O5\">touched_whale</field></block></value><next><block type=\"typescript_statement\"><mutation xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" line0=\"killer_whale = null\" numlines=\"1\"></mutation><next><block type=\"function_call\"><mutation name=\"play_whale_sound\" functionid=\"$oI[!GM$]W(or4nl?y^}\"></mutation><next><block type=\"hudChangeScoreBy\"><value name=\"value\"><shadow type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">10</field></shadow></value><next><block type=\"hudChangeLifeBy\"><value name=\"value\"><shadow type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">1</field></shadow></value><next><block type=\"controls_if\"><value name=\"IF0\"><shadow type=\"logic_boolean\"><field name=\"BOOL\">TRUE</field></shadow><block type=\"logic_compare\"><field name=\"OP\">GT</field><value name=\"A\"><shadow type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">0</field></shadow><block type=\"hudLife\"></block></value><value name=\"B\"><shadow type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">3</field></shadow></value></block></value><statement name=\"DO0\"><block type=\"hudSetLife\"><value name=\"value\"><shadow type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">3</field></shadow></value></block></statement></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></statement><value name=\"IF1\"><shadow type=\"logic_boolean\"><field name=\"BOOL\">TRUE</field></shadow><block type=\"variables_get\"><field name=\"VAR\" id=\"Quy^%gw@YD8:xGD#l62e\">can_take_damage</field></block></value><statement name=\"DO1\"><block type=\"variables_set\"><field name=\"VAR\" id=\"Quy^%gw@YD8:xGD#l62e\">can_take_damage</field><value name=\"VALUE\"><shadow type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">0</field></shadow><block type=\"logic_boolean\"><field name=\"BOOL\">FALSE</field></block></value><next><block type=\"hudChangeLifeBy\"><value name=\"value\"><shadow type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">-1</field></shadow></value><next><block type=\"camerashake\"><value name=\"amplitude\"><shadow type=\"math_number_minmax\"><mutation min=\"1\" max=\"8\" label=\"Amplitude\" precision=\"0\"></mutation><field name=\"SLIDER\">4</field></shadow></value><value name=\"duration\"><shadow type=\"timePicker\"><field name=\"ms\">200</field></shadow></value><next><block type=\"function_call\"><mutation name=\"play_damage_sound\" functionid=\"*L-,8cWemG%iyqUM*h)R\"></mutation><next><block type=\"device_pause\"><value name=\"pause\"><shadow type=\"timePicker\"><field name=\"ms\">1500</field></shadow></value><next><block type=\"variables_set\"><field name=\"VAR\" id=\"Quy^%gw@YD8:xGD#l62e\">can_take_damage</field><value name=\"VALUE\"><shadow type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">0</field></shadow><block type=\"logic_boolean\"><field name=\"BOOL\">TRUE</field></block></value></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></statement></block></statement></block><block type=\"function_definition\" x=\"1861\" y=\"2858\"><mutation name=\"play_growth_sound\" functionid=\"II5lTnWuqqmQVC,xllKK\"></mutation><field name=\"function_name\">play_growth_sound</field><comment pinned=\"false\" h=\"80\" w=\"160\">Reference: https://arcade.makecode.com/reference/info/on-countdown-end\nThe reference runs a function when the countdown reaches zero.\nMy code registers on_countdown_end to play the ending sound, read the score, show it in a message, and finish the game with game.game_over(True). (game over screen)\nReference: https://arcade.makecode.com/reference/info/high-score\nThe reference retrieves the recorded best score with info.high_score().\nMy code saves it before the run and compares final_score against that value.\nA higher score, or a previous best of 0, selects \"NEW HIGH SCORE!\"\notherwise the message challenges the player to beat the previous best score.\n============================================================================================================================================================================\n============================================================================================================================================================================\nReference: https://arcade.makecode.com/reference/music/play-tone\n7. GROWTH SOUND</comment><statement name=\"STACK\"><block type=\"mixer_play_note\"><value name=\"note\"><shadow type=\"device_note\"><field name=\"note\">523</field></shadow></value><value name=\"duration\"><shadow type=\"device_beat\"><field name=\"fraction\">BeatFraction.Half</field></shadow><block type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">70</field></block></value><next><block type=\"mixer_play_note\"><value name=\"note\"><shadow type=\"device_note\"><field name=\"note\">659</field></shadow></value><value name=\"duration\"><shadow type=\"device_beat\"><field name=\"fraction\">BeatFraction.Half</field></shadow><block type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">70</field></block></value><next><block type=\"mixer_play_note\"><value name=\"note\"><shadow type=\"device_note\"><field name=\"note\">784</field></shadow></value><value name=\"duration\"><shadow type=\"device_beat\"><field name=\"fraction\">BeatFraction.Half</field></shadow><block type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">130</field></block></value></block></next></block></next></block></statement></block><block type=\"function_definition\" x=\"2243\" y=\"2858\"><mutation name=\"play_whale_sound\" functionid=\"$oI[!GM$]W(or4nl?y^}\"></mutation><field name=\"function_name\">play_whale_sound</field><comment pinned=\"false\" h=\"80\" w=\"160\">The reference explains how frequency controls pitch and milliseconds control length.\nMy code uses falling pitches of 523, 392 and 262 Hz for 120, 120 and 250 ms.\nThe longer final tone marks the end of the two minute countdown.\n============================================================================================================================================================================\n============================================================================================================================================================================\n9. KILLER WHALE SOUND</comment><statement name=\"STACK\"><block type=\"mixer_play_note\"><value name=\"note\"><shadow type=\"device_note\"><field name=\"note\">523</field></shadow></value><value name=\"duration\"><shadow type=\"device_beat\"><field name=\"fraction\">BeatFraction.Half</field></shadow><block type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">70</field></block></value><next><block type=\"mixer_play_note\"><value name=\"note\"><shadow type=\"device_note\"><field name=\"note\">784</field></shadow></value><value name=\"duration\"><shadow type=\"device_beat\"><field name=\"fraction\">BeatFraction.Half</field></shadow><block type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">70</field></block></value><next><block type=\"mixer_play_note\"><value name=\"note\"><shadow type=\"device_note\"><field name=\"note\">1047</field></shadow></value><value name=\"duration\"><shadow type=\"device_beat\"><field name=\"fraction\">BeatFraction.Half</field></shadow><block type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">130</field></block></value></block></next></block></next></block></statement></block><block type=\"function_definition\" x=\"2630\" y=\"2858\"><mutation name=\"change_shark_image\" functionid=\"zs;e#~YE{1,j79AZUmD+\"><arg name=\"new_image\" id=\"a3zsfd7kkoog1zfealzc\" type=\"Image\"></arg></mutation><field name=\"function_name\">change_shark_image</field><comment pinned=\"false\" h=\"80\" w=\"160\">Reference: https://arcade.makecode.com/reference/sprites/on-overlap\nThe reference runs a handler when two chosen sprite kinds touch.\nMy code selects player and KillerWhale, then checks shark_level:\nlevel 3 eats the whale for 10 points: lower levels take damage without removing the whale.\nReference: https://arcade.makecode.com/reference/info/change-life-by\nThe reference adds life with positive values and removes it with negative values.\nMy code uses 1 for eating and -1 for damage, with a separate 3 heart cap.\nThe shared can_take_damage flag and pause also protect against repeated hits.\n============================================================================================================================================================================\n============================================================================================================================================================================\n11. CHANGE SHARK IMAGE\nnew_image is the picture passed into this function when the shark grows.\nThe direction check keeps the new shark picture facing the same way as before.</comment><value name=\"a3zsfd7kkoog1zfealzc\"><block type=\"argument_reporter_custom\" deletable=\"false\"><mutation typename=\"Image\"></mutation><field name=\"VALUE\">new_image</field></block></value><statement name=\"STACK\"><block type=\"spritesetimage\"><value name=\"sprite\"><block type=\"variables_get\"><field name=\"VAR\" id=\"y#m,e55f;dM@?7=%5#2B\">shark</field></block></value><value name=\"img\"><shadow type=\"screen_image_picker\"><field name=\"img\"></field></shadow><block type=\"Image_clone\"><value name=\"picture\"><block type=\"argument_reporter_custom\"><mutation typename=\"Image\"></mutation><field name=\"VALUE\">new_image</field></block></value></block></value><next><block type=\"controls_if\"><value name=\"IF0\"><shadow type=\"logic_boolean\"><field name=\"BOOL\">TRUE</field></shadow><block type=\"logic_negate\"><value name=\"BOOL\"><shadow type=\"logic_boolean\"><field name=\"BOOL\">TRUE</field></shadow><block type=\"variables_get\"><field name=\"VAR\" id=\"qY6.xn)iO0yb,?JoHi1F\">shark_facing_right</field></block></value></block></value><statement name=\"DO0\"><block type=\"Image_flipX\"><value name=\"picture\"><block type=\"spriteimage\"><value name=\"sprite\"><block type=\"variables_get\"><field name=\"VAR\" id=\"y#m,e55f;dM@?7=%5#2B\">shark</field></block></value></block></value></block></statement></block></next></block></statement></block><block type=\"function_definition\" x=\"3140\" y=\"2858\"><mutation name=\"play_small_fish_sound\" functionid=\"qGX`U;]}{b[=votR^j*M\"></mutation><field name=\"function_name\">play_small_fish_sound</field><comment pinned=\"false\" h=\"80\" w=\"160\">Reference: https://arcade.makecode.com/reference/sprites/sprite/set-image\nThe reference replaces a sprite's picture with set_image().\nMy code gives the shark its new growth image through this function.\nReference: https://arcade.makecode.com/reference/images/image/clone\nThe reference copies an image with clone(): my code copies the growth artwork\nbefore using it so flipping the shark does not change the original image.\nReference: https://arcade.makecode.com/reference/images/image/flip-x\nThe reference mirrors an image horizontally with flip_x().\nMy code flips the new right facing artwork if shark_facing_right is False.\n============================================================================================================================================================================\n============================================================================================================================================================================\n12. SMALL FISH SOUND</comment><statement name=\"STACK\"><block type=\"mixer_play_note\"><value name=\"note\"><shadow type=\"device_note\"><field name=\"note\">784</field></shadow></value><value name=\"duration\"><shadow type=\"device_beat\"><field name=\"fraction\">BeatFraction.Half</field></shadow><block type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">80</field></block></value></block></statement></block><block type=\"function_definition\" x=\"3560\" y=\"2858\"><mutation name=\"play_big_fish_sound\" functionid=\"*bxy}5{m1=oUh-;l,Ozj\"></mutation><field name=\"function_name\">play_big_fish_sound</field><comment pinned=\"false\" h=\"80\" w=\"160\">The reference shows how to play a tone by setting its pitch and duration.\nMy code uses 147 Hz for a low tone and 180 milliseconds for a short sound.\nThis function is called when a big fish or killer whale damages the shark.\n============================================================================================================================================================================\n============================================================================================================================================================================\n3. BIG FISH SOUND</comment><statement name=\"STACK\"><block type=\"mixer_play_note\"><value name=\"note\"><shadow type=\"device_note\"><field name=\"note\">659</field></shadow></value><value name=\"duration\"><shadow type=\"device_beat\"><field name=\"fraction\">BeatFraction.Half</field></shadow><block type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">70</field></block></value><next><block type=\"mixer_play_note\"><value name=\"note\"><shadow type=\"device_note\"><field name=\"note\">880</field></shadow></value><value name=\"duration\"><shadow type=\"device_beat\"><field name=\"fraction\">BeatFraction.Half</field></shadow><block type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">100</field></block></value></block></next></block></statement></block><block type=\"function_definition\" x=\"3961\" y=\"2858\"><mutation name=\"play_damage_sound\" functionid=\"*L-,8cWemG%iyqUM*h)R\"></mutation><field name=\"function_name\">play_damage_sound</field><comment pinned=\"false\" h=\"80\" w=\"160\">Reference: https://arcade.makecode.com/reference/sprites/sprite/set-kin\nThe \"Sprite kinds\" example uses SpriteKind.create() to define new categories.\nMy code names these SmallFish, BigFish and KillerWhale because each creature can have its own collision rules.\n:each fish type has differnt rules for what happens when it touchs the shark\n============================================================================================================================================================================\n============================================================================================================================================================================\nReference used when creating game sound: https://arcade.makecode.com/reference/music/play-tone\n2. DAMAGE SOUND</comment><statement name=\"STACK\"><block type=\"mixer_play_note\"><value name=\"note\"><shadow type=\"device_note\"><field name=\"note\">147</field></shadow></value><value name=\"duration\"><shadow type=\"device_beat\"><field name=\"fraction\">BeatFraction.Half</field></shadow><block type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">180</field></block></value></block></statement></block><block type=\"function_definition\" x=\"4343\" y=\"2858\"><mutation name=\"play_time_up_sound\" functionid=\"6:9=gz8#~?5ev]w:!HZP\"></mutation><field name=\"function_name\">play_time_up_sound</field><comment pinned=\"false\" h=\"80\" w=\"160\">The reference plays one tone using a frequency and a duration.\nMy code joins 523, 659 and 784 Hz tones lasting 70, 70 and 130 ms.\nThis rising sequence is called when the shark grows to level 2 or 3.\n============================================================================================================================================================================\n============================================================================================================================================================================\n8. TIME-UP SOUND</comment><statement name=\"STACK\"><block type=\"mixer_play_note\"><value name=\"note\"><shadow type=\"device_note\"><field name=\"note\">523</field></shadow></value><value name=\"duration\"><shadow type=\"device_beat\"><field name=\"fraction\">BeatFraction.Half</field></shadow><block type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">120</field></block></value><next><block type=\"mixer_play_note\"><value name=\"note\"><shadow type=\"device_note\"><field name=\"note\">392</field></shadow></value><value name=\"duration\"><shadow type=\"device_beat\"><field name=\"fraction\">BeatFraction.Half</field></shadow><block type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">120</field></block></value><next><block type=\"mixer_play_note\"><value name=\"note\"><shadow type=\"device_note\"><field name=\"note\">262</field></shadow></value><value name=\"duration\"><shadow type=\"device_beat\"><field name=\"fraction\">BeatFraction.Half</field></shadow><block type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">250</field></block></value></block></next></block></next></block></statement></block></xml>","main.ts":"","README.md":" ","assets.json":"","main.py":"@namespace\nclass SpriteKind:\n    SmallFish = SpriteKind.create()\n    BigFish = SpriteKind.create()\n    KillerWhale = SpriteKind.create()\n# Reference: https://arcade.makecode.com/reference/sprites/sprite/set-kin\n# The \"Sprite kinds\" example uses SpriteKind.create() to define new categories.\n# My code names these SmallFish, BigFish and KillerWhale because each creature can have its own collision rules.\n# :each fish type has differnt rules for what happens when it touchs the shark\n# ============================================================================================================================================================================\n# ============================================================================================================================================================================\n# Reference used when creating game sound: https://arcade.makecode.com/reference/music/play-tone\n# 2. DAMAGE SOUND\ndef play_damage_sound():\n    music.play_tone(147, 180)\n# The reference shows how to play a tone by setting its pitch and duration.\n# My code uses 147 Hz for a low tone and 180 milliseconds for a short sound.\n# This function is called when a big fish or killer whale damages the shark.\n# ============================================================================================================================================================================\n# ============================================================================================================================================================================\n# 3. BIG FISH SOUND\ndef play_big_fish_sound():\n    music.play_tone(659, 70)\n    music.play_tone(880, 100)\n# The reference explains the pitch and duration inputs for music.play_tone().\n# My code calls it twice: 659 Hz for 70 ms, then 880 Hz for 100 ms.\n# The rising sound plays when the shark eats a big fish.\n# ============================================================================================================================================================================\n# ============================================================================================================================================================================\n# 4. BIG FISH COLLISION\n# This function runs when the shark touches a big fish.\n# Touched_fish is the particular big fish that the shark has touched.\n# The game checks the shark level before deciding whether to eat the fish or lose a heart.\n\ndef on_on_overlap(player_sprite, touched_fish):\n    global big_fish, can_take_damage\n    if shark_level >= 2:\n        sprites.destroy(touched_fish)\n        big_fish = None\n        play_big_fish_sound()\n        info.change_score_by(3)\n        info.change_life_by(1)\n        if info.life() > 3:\n            info.set_life(3)\n    elif can_take_damage:\n        can_take_damage = False\n        info.change_life_by(-1)\n        scene.camera_shake(4, 200)\n        play_damage_sound()\n        pause(1500)\n        can_take_damage = True\nsprites.on_overlap(SpriteKind.player, SpriteKind.BigFish, on_on_overlap)\n\n# Reference: https://arcade.makecode.com/reference/sprites/on-overlap\n# The reference connects two sprite kinds to a collision function.\n# My code connects player and BigFish to on_on_overlap, then adds a level check\n# level 2 or higher eats the fish for 3 points: level 1 loses one heart.\n# The fish is destroyed only its eaten (damage does not remove it)\n# Reference: https://arcade.makecode.com/reference/loops/pause\n# The reference uses pause() to delay this part of the program.\n# My code uses pause(1500) after the damage sound, with can_take_damage False, then restores the flag to prevent repeated damage during that wait.\n# # can_take_damage is set to False to stop more fish or whale hits during the wait, after the sound and a 1.5 second pause, it becomes True again.\n# ============================================================================================================================================================================\n# ============================================================================================================================================================================\n# 5. SMALL FISH COLLISION + growing to level 2\n# Small fish can be eaten at level 1 and at every later level.\n# The game removes only the small fish that was touched.\n# The growth check happens after the point is added, so eating the 20th small fish\n\ndef on_on_overlap2(player_sprite3, touched_fish2):\n    global shark_level\n    sprites.destroy(touched_fish2)\n    play_small_fish_sound()\n    info.change_score_by(1)\n    info.change_life_by(1)\n    if info.life() > 3:\n        info.set_life(3)\n    if info.score() >= 20 and shark_level == 1:\n        shark_level = 2\n        change_shark_image(assets.image(\"\"\"\n            Medium Shark new\n            \"\"\"))\n        play_growth_sound()\nsprites.on_overlap(SpriteKind.player, SpriteKind.SmallFish, on_on_overlap2)\n\n# Reference: https://arcade.makecode.com/reference/sprites/on-overlap\n# The reference passes the two overlapping sprites into a handler.\n# My code receives the small fish as touched_fish2 and removes that eaten fish.\n# Reference: https://arcade.makecode.com/reference/info/change-score-by\n# The reference changes the score by the supplied amount: my code uses 1.\n# I added rules restore one heart, cap health at 3, and grow a level 1 shark to level 2 when the score reaches 20.\n# Its picture changes to the medium shark and the growth sound plays.\n# ============================================================================================================================================================================\n# ============================================================================================================================================================================\n# 6. TWO-MINUTE TIMER\n# This runs when the countdown finishes, not when a fish is eaten.\n# str(final_score) turns the score into text so it can appear in the message.\n# A score equal to a nonzero previous best does not count as a new high score here.\n\ndef on_countdown_end():\n    global final_score\n    music.stop_all_sounds()\n    play_time_up_sound()\n    final_score = info.score()\n    game.splash(\"TIME'S UP!\", \"Your score: \" + (\"\" + str(final_score)))\n    if best_score_before_run == 0 or final_score > best_score_before_run:\n        game.set_game_over_message(True, \"NEW HIGH SCORE!\")\n    else:\n        game.set_game_over_message(True, \"BEAT \" + (\"\" + str(best_score_before_run)) + \" NEXT!\")\n    game.game_over(True)\ninfo.on_countdown_end(on_countdown_end)\n\n# Reference: https://arcade.makecode.com/reference/info/on-countdown-end\n# The reference runs a function when the countdown reaches zero.\n# My code registers on_countdown_end to play the ending sound, read the score, show it in a message, and finish the game with game.game_over(True). (game over screen)\n# Reference: https://arcade.makecode.com/reference/info/high-score\n# The reference retrieves the recorded best score with info.high_score().\n# My code saves it before the run and compares final_score against that value.\n# A higher score, or a previous best of 0, selects \"NEW HIGH SCORE!\"\n# otherwise the message challenges the player to beat the previous best score.\n# ============================================================================================================================================================================\n# ============================================================================================================================================================================\n# Reference: https://arcade.makecode.com/reference/music/play-tone\n# 7. GROWTH SOUND\ndef play_growth_sound():\n    music.play_tone(523, 70)\n    music.play_tone(659, 70)\n    music.play_tone(784, 130)\n# The reference plays one tone using a frequency and a duration.\n# My code joins 523, 659 and 784 Hz tones lasting 70, 70 and 130 ms.\n# This rising sequence is called when the shark grows to level 2 or 3.\n# ============================================================================================================================================================================\n# ============================================================================================================================================================================\n# 8. TIME-UP SOUND\ndef play_time_up_sound():\n    music.play_tone(523, 120)\n    music.play_tone(392, 120)\n    music.play_tone(262, 250)\n# The reference explains how frequency controls pitch and milliseconds control length.\n# My code uses falling pitches of 523, 392 and 262 Hz for 120, 120 and 250 ms.\n# The longer final tone marks the end of the two minute countdown.\n# ========================================================================================================================================